  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "With an integer array **sorted** in non-decreasing order, there is exactly one integer in the array that occurs more than 25% of the time, output that integer.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n```\nInput: arr = [1,2,2,6,6,6,6,7,10]\nOutput: 6\n```\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n```\nInput: arr = [1,1]\nOutput: 1\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `1 <= arr.length <= 104`\n* `0 <= arr[i] <= 105`",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
